----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART V2 -- THE ATTACK: the term B3b omits, and it is the one that is measured
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The Sun is not isolated.  g_ext = 2.146e-10 m/s^2 > a_0, so the nonlinear MOND field equation's
  exterior boundary condition imprints a CONSTANT anomalous quadrupole on the whole interior:
      delta-Phi = -(Q_2/2)[(e.x)^2 - x^2/3]   ->   a_i = Q_2[(e.x) e_i - x_i/3]
  (Milgrom 2009 MNRAS 399 474; Blanchet & Novak 2011 arXiv:1105.5815; Hees+2014 PRD 89 102002.)
  Q_2 is set at r_M ~ 8000 AU where y ~ 1.  Route A's exponential does NOTHING to it -- that is
  g04's own A5b finding, which FAILS at 5.8x over the Park+2026 ceiling.  The anomalous acceleration
  it carries is Q_2 * r, GROWING outward, ANISOTROPIC, and it precesses perihelia.

  V2.0 -- MUTATION CONTROL M2: Q_2 = 0 must give exactly zero through the quadrupole path
  [PASS] V2a  MUTATION CONTROL M2: the quadrupole path returns identically zero at Q_2 = 0   (max |dw| over 6 planets x 3 orientations at Q_2 = 0 is 0.0e+00; the Q_2 = 1e-26 reference at Saturn is 6.349e-10 rad/orbit.  No spurious constant is leaking into the quadrupole branch)

  V2.1 -- ANCHOR: invert the measured sigmas to a Q_2 ceiling; must land on the PUBLISHED one
  If this machinery is right, feeding each planet's measured sigma(omegadot) back through it must
  reproduce the Q_2 ceilings the literature actually quotes (Park+2026 5.2e-27, Hees+2014 9e-27).
  Nothing is tuned: the geometry is scanned over the full range of orientations and the resulting
  per-planet ceiling BAND is compared to the published number.
  planet      P [yr]  |dw/dt| per Q2 [mas/yr / (1e-26 s^-2)]    Q2 ceiling from sigma [s^-2]
  Mercury       0.24                   2.538e-06 - 1.156e-04             5.19e-25 - 2.36e-23
  Venus         0.62                   6.625e-06 - 3.017e-04             4.97e-25 - 2.26e-23
  Earth         1.00                   1.077e-05 - 4.903e-04             3.87e-26 - 1.76e-24
  Mars          1.88                   2.017e-05 - 9.183e-04             4.03e-27 - 1.83e-25
  Jupiter      11.87                   1.277e-04 - 5.813e-03             4.82e-25 - 2.19e-23
  Saturn       29.45                   3.167e-04 - 1.442e-02             3.26e-27 - 1.48e-25
  [PASS] V2b  ANCHOR: the published Q_2 ceiling falls inside the band this machinery derives from Saturn   (Saturn's measured sigma = 0.0047 mas/yr maps to Q_2 <= 3.26e-27 - 1.48e-25 s^-2 across orbit orientations, and the published ceilings -- Park+2026 5.2e-27 and Hees+2014 9.0e-27 -- sit inside that band.  Saturn is exactly the planet those analyses are driven by (Cassini ranging).  The quadrupole precession machinery is therefore validated against published numbers it was not fitted to, which is what licenses the next check)

