  Route A's Q_2 = 3.00e-26 (canonical) / 3.27e-26 (alt) s^-2, taken
  from g04's own A5b (Desmond+2024 eq 12, pinned to 0.76% on that paper's anchors for THIS kernel).
  planet      MG quadrupole rate [mas/yr]   sigma [mas/yr]   over by   B3b isolated tail   omitted factor
  Mercury                      3.4676e-04          0.00600       0.1             1e-7399           1e7395
  Venus                        9.0505e-04          0.01500       0.1             1e-4737           1e4734
  Earth                        1.4710e-03          0.00190       0.8             1e-3391           1e3388
  Mars                         2.7550e-03          0.00037       7.4             1e-2067           1e2064
  Jupiter                      1.7439e-02          0.28000       0.1              1e-626            1e624
  Saturn                       4.3265e-02          0.00470       9.2              1e-336            1e335
  [FAIL] V2c  B3b's 'largest modified-gravity precession rate anywhere inside 100 AU' is the largest   (IT IS NOT, BY TWELVE TO FOURTEEN ORDERS.  At the very configuration B3b names -- a = 100 AU, e = 0.9 -- the external-field quadrupole gives 6.41e-01 mas/yr against B3b's 1.89e-14 mas/yr for the isolated tail: a factor 10^14.  At Saturn the quadrupole gives up to 0.0433 mas/yr against sigma = 0.0047.  B3b computed ONE TERM of the modified-gravity solution -- the isolated-Sun central tail -- and its sentence promotes that to 'the modified-gravity precession')
  [FAIL] V2d  the modified-gravity arm's inner-solar-system precession is below the measured bounds   (IT IS NOT.  Route A's Q_2 exceeds the sharpest per-planet perihelion sigma by up to 9.2x (canonical) / 10.0x (alt) at the maximal-coupling orientation.  That is the SAME 5.8x/6.3x g04's A5b reports against the Park+2026 ceiling, recovered here through perihelion precession rather than through the Cassini Q_2 fit -- so the modified-gravity arm does not merely have magnitude to work with inside 100 AU, it has too much, and the inner solar system already excludes it.  (Reading caveat carried from g04: the true orientation is fixed by the Galactic-centre direction, not scanned, and the significance is set by the Milky Way mass model -- Desmond+2024 quote 8.7 sigma fiducial, 1.9 sigma with bulge galaxies cut.  The ROBUST statement is 'of order the bound, not 1e-10 of it'))

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART V3 -- does the inner solar system decide the fork, or not?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  modified GRAVITY  arm : Q_2 = 3.00e-26 s^-2  ->  5.8x the Park+2026 ceiling
  modified INERTIA  arm : Q_2 = 7.40e-34 s^-2  ->  1.4e-07 of the same ceiling
                          (committed in cassini_mi_evasion_2026/, on the OLD kernel; quoted, not
                           recomputed, exactly as g04 flags it)
  [FAIL] V3a  the fork CANNOT be decided by orbital dynamics in the inner solar system   (IT CAN, AND g04's OWN PART A DECIDES IT.  The two arms differ by a factor 4.1e+07 in the one inner-solar-system observable that carries magnitude, and the measurement sits BETWEEN them: the modified-gravity arm is 5.8x OVER the 2-sigma ceiling and the modified-inertia arm is 1e-07 UNDER it.  A bracketed measurement is the definition of a decided fork.  g04's own conclusion says so -- 'the fork-relevant solar-system information is entirely in A5b (Q_2)' -- which is precisely what the B3b headline sentence denies)
  orbit-shape dependence of the quadrupole precession: orientation spread at fixed (a,e) = 45.5x;  e=0.90 / e=0.01 at fixed beta, a = 100 AU = 0.44x
  [FAIL] V3b  the Q_2 channel is orbit-shape-blind, so 'cannot be decided by ORBIT SHAPE' still stands   (IT IS NOT ORBIT-SHAPE-BLIND.  The quadrupole force is anisotropic, so its perihelion advance depends on the perihelion's orientation relative to the symmetry axis (Saturn response varies 45.5x over the orientation scan at fixed a and e) and on eccentricity (0.44x between e = 0.01 and e = 0.90 at a = 100 AU, fixed beta).  Both are far from 1, which is what 'blind' would require.  Orbit shape is exactly the handle the published Q_2 constraints use -- they are fits to SUPPLEMENTARY PERIHELION ADVANCES, per planet, per geometry.  The eccentricity lever here is modest (0.44x, not 1e157) but it is not zero, and it sits on a signal that is of order the measurement rather than 1e-10 of it, which is the whole point)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART V4 -- the confound lens: would ordinary cold dark matter give the same signature?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  For the B3b NULL: GR + CDM predicts identically zero solar-system anomaly.  1.9e-14 mas/yr is
  observationally indistinguishable from zero, so B3b separates the framework from nothing.
  For the Q_2 CHANNEL: the Newtonian/CDM Galactic tide at the Sun is of order V^2/R_0^2 =
  8.48e-31 s^-2 (V = 233 km/s, R_0 = 8.2 kpc), against the Park+2026 ceiling 5.2e-27 and
  Route A's 3.00e-26.  The CDM tide is 6132x BELOW the ceiling
  and 3.5e+04x below the MOND value.
  [FAIL] V4a  the B3b null discriminates the framework from GR + cold dark matter   (IT DOES NOT, and cannot: 1.9e-14 mas/yr is zero to any instrument.  B3b is a CONSISTENCY statement, not a discriminant.  This is not a criticism of the arithmetic -- g04's own honesty note says the same -- but it does mean B3b carries no fork information in EITHER direction, so nothing about the fork can be concluded from it)
  [FAIL] V4b  the Q_2 channel is confounded by the ordinary Newtonian Galactic tide   (IT IS NOT.  The CDM/Newtonian tide 8.48e-31 s^-2 is 6132x below the measurement ceiling and 3.5e+04x below Route A's prediction, so the Q_2 excess is not something ordinary cold dark matter produces.  The channel that DOES carry magnitude inside 100 AU is therefore clean of the confound the audit lens asks about -- which makes the refutation of B3b's inference stronger, not weaker)

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================

 THE ARITHMETIC SURVIVES.  Route A's isolated-Sun central tail gives 1.89e-14 mas/yr at a = 100 AU,
 e = 0.9 -- 10^10 below Mars -- reproduced here to 0.004 dex with a different quadrature,
 a transverse term g04 does not carry, and a mutation control that fires at 33973x on the retired
 kernel.  The 10^157 ratio at 10 AU is confirmed to 0.005 dex.  V1a-V1d all PASS.

 THE INFERENCE DOES NOT.  "The modified-gravity precession has no magnitude to work with [inside 100 AU],
 so the fork cannot be decided by orbit shape in the inner solar system" is false on both clauses:

  * The isolated-Sun tail is one term of the modified-gravity solution, and not the leading one.  The
    Sun sits in a Galactic field above a_0; the resulting anomalous quadrupole is set at r_M ~ 8000 AU
    where the exponential does nothing, and inside 100 AU it exceeds the isolated tail by
    10^14.  Fed through the same Gauss machinery -- anchored by recovering the PUBLISHED Q_2
    ceilings out of the measured per-planet sigmas (V2b) -- Route A's own Q_2 gives up to 9.2x the
    sharpest per-planet perihelion sigma.  The modified-gravity arm is not invisible inside 100 AU; it
    is already EXCLUDED there.

  * The fork IS decided there.  The two arms sit at 5.8x over and 1e-07 under the same ceiling, a
    separation of 4.1e+07, and the measurement falls between them.  g04's own A5b FAILS and g04's own
    conclusion says the fork-relevant solar-system information is entirely in that check.  The B3b
    headline sentence contradicts the file it is drawn from.

  * And the quadrupole IS an orbit-shape observable: the published constraints are fits to
    supplementary perihelion advances planet by planet, and the response varies with e and with the
    perihelion's orientation.

 WHAT SHOULD BE CLAIMED INSTEAD.  "Route A's ISOLATED-SUN exponential tail is vacuous as an eccentricity
 discriminant inside 100 AU, by 10^10 -- and this says nothing about the fork, because the inner solar
 system's fork-relevant signal is the external-field quadrupole, which is 5.8x over the bound for
 modified gravity and 1e-7 under it for modified inertia."  That sentence is fully supported by g04.
 The one that was handed out is not.

 DIRECTION OF THE ERROR.  Against the framework's operative arm, not for it.  Every correction here makes
 the modified-gravity arm's solar-system standing WORSE.  Nothing in this file is a win for anything.

 CAVEATS, LOAD-BEARING.
  * Q_2 = 3.00e-26 s^-2 is QUOTED from g04's A5b, not recomputed.  If that integral is wrong, V2c/V2d/V3a
    move with it.  It is pinned to 0.76% on Desmond+2024's own published anchors for this exact kernel.
  * The Q_2 -> precession response is computed with the symmetry axis IN the orbit plane and scanned over
    orientation.  The true Galactic-centre direction is fixed and out of the ecliptic, so the real
    per-planet response is a specific number inside the band, not the maximum.  Every "over by" figure is
    therefore an UPPER reading; the robust statement is "of order the measured bound", which is all the
    refutation needs -- B3b's claim is 1e-10 of the bound.
  * The MI contrast 7.4e-34 s^-2 is committed on the OLD kernel nu = sqrt(1+1/y) and quoted, not
    recomputed, exactly as g04 flags.  The fork separation in V3a inherits that.
  * Nothing here prefers the framework over LambdaCDM.  V4a/V4b establish only that the Q_2 channel is
    not CDM-confounded, i.e. that it is a real discriminant against the framework's modified-gravity arm.


RESULT: 12 checks, 6 FAIL -> ["V2c  B3b's 'largest modified-gravity precession rate anywhere inside 100 AU' is the largest", "V2d  the modified-gravity arm's inner-solar-system precession is below the measured bounds", 'V3a  the fork CANNOT be decided by orbital dynamics in the inner solar system', "V3b  the Q_2 channel is orbit-shape-blind, so 'cannot be decided by ORBIT SHAPE' still stands", 'V4a  the B3b null discriminates the framework from GR + cold dark matter', 'V4b  the Q_2 channel is confounded by the ordinary Newtonian Galactic tide']   rc=1
